{"source":"github","project_id":"baguette","target":"tidymodels/baguette","id":"pr/91","ref":91,"title":"Register C5.0 and earth engine arguments","description":"Registers dials tuning parameters for engine arguments with `parsnip::set_model_arg()` so they can be tuned.\n\n- **`bag_tree()` / C5.0:** `CF` (`confidence_factor()`), `noGlobalPruning` (`no_global_pruning()`), `winnow` (`predictor_winnowing()`), `fuzzyThreshold` (`fuzzy_thresholding()`).\n  - These are passed into `C50::C5.0Control()` by `make_c5_spec()`.\n  - `bands` is not registered; it only applies to rule-based models.\n- **`bag_mars()` / earth:** `nk` (`max_num_terms()`).\n\nAdds `dials (\u003e= 0.0.8)`.","published_at":"2026-11-02T18:39:45Z","updated_at":"2026-11-02T21:58:28Z","url":"https://github.com/tidymodels/baguette/pull/91","type":"pr","extra":{"author":"topepo","merged_at":"2026-11-02T21:58:28Z","state":"MERGED"}}
{"source":"github","project_id":"baguette","target":"tidymodels/baguette","id":"pr/89","ref":89,"title":"Update Plausible analytics snippet","description":"## Summary\r\n\r\n- Replace the old Plausible `\u003cscript defer data-domain=...\u003e` tag with the new async snippet that includes `plausible.init()`\r\n\r\n## Context\r\n\r\nPlausible has updated their recommended tracking snippet. The new format uses `async` loading with an inline init script, and no longer requires the `data-domain` attribute.\r\n","published_at":"2026-04-09T11:57:44Z","updated_at":"2026-11-02T21:57:47Z","url":"https://github.com/tidymodels/baguette/pull/89","type":"pr","extra":{"author":"jeroenjanssens","merged_at":"2026-11-02T21:57:47Z","state":"MERGED"}}
